192
00:13:56,566 --> 00:14:01,235
The reference page adds nothing new. Then
separate two lists: what you set for

193
00:14:01,275 --> 00:14:05,822
yourself, and what a team should agree
on and enforce somewhere other than a

194
00:14:05,862 --> 00:14:06,667
personal file.

195
00:14:08,507 --> 00:14:10,155
Five mistakes to watch for.

196
00:14:10,495 --> 00:14:15,222
Defending a rule with "best practice". Root
cause: the mechanism that pays for the

197
00:14:15,262 --> 00:14:19,233
rule was never stated, so the rule
has no defense when it costs time.

198
00:14:19,573 --> 00:14:24,249
Enforcing the convention and forgetting
the truth. Root cause: a linter checks the

199
00:14:24,289 --> 00:14:27,528
form of a message, and form
does not make a message true.

200
00:14:27,868 --> 00:14:32,714
Squash-merging large pull requests. Root
cause: the squash makes the pull request

201
00:14:32,754 --> 00:14:37,781
the unit of undo, so one mistake can only
be reverted together with everything else.

202
00:14:38,121 --> 00:14:41,517
Treating "Request changes" or
CODEOWNERS as enforcement.

203
00:14:41,557 --> 00:14:46,303
Root cause: review is a practice; only
a ruleset turns it into a condition the

204
00:14:46,343 --> 00:14:47,162
server checks.

205
00:14:47,502 --> 00:14:50,525
Reporting a squash-merged
branch as abandoned work.

206
00:14:50,565 --> 00:14:55,571
Root cause: commit-based checks test ancestry
and patch identity, and a squash keeps

207
00:14:55,611 --> 00:14:57,613
the content while discarding both.

