00:15:13,500 --> 00:15:18,225
distances, tag positions, the fix-direction
check on each release branch, the

212
00:15:18,265 --> 00:15:22,371
largest blobs in history, the short
subjects, the signature status.

213
00:15:22,711 --> 00:15:27,071
Her report has one line per finding, each
with the command that produced it and the

214
00:15:27,111 --> 00:15:30,517
practice it relates to. She doesn't
write "the history is messy".

215
00:15:30,857 --> 00:15:35,720
She writes three things. A fix exists on
one release branch with no equivalent on

216
00:15:35,760 --> 00:15:40,683
main, and she gives the commit ID. One
branch reported as unmerged has its content

217
00:15:40,723 --> 00:15:45,344
on main already and can be deleted. And
a file of two megabytes is in history

218
00:15:45,384 --> 00:15:50,186
although it is no longer tracked. Each
finding ends with a control and the layer

219
00:15:50,226 --> 00:15:54,968
that would enforce it. The CTO reads it
in five minutes and approves two of the

220
00:15:55,008 --> 00:15:58,418
controls the same day, because
each came with its reason.

