229
00:16:36,381 --> 00:16:39,534
Answer out loud. The word
that matters is "mechanism".

230
00:16:39,574 --> 00:16:44,265
A strong answer gives, for each of the
three, a fact about how Git works and the

231
00:16:44,305 --> 00:16:47,636
concrete operation that the
practice makes cheap or safe.

232
00:16:47,676 --> 00:16:51,421
For small commits, name the
operations whose unit is the commit.

233
00:16:51,461 --> 00:16:56,093
For force pushes, describe the state of
a colleague's clone afterwards and what

234
00:16:56,133 --> 00:16:57,986
their next ordinary action does.

235
00:16:58,326 --> 00:17:02,775
For inspection, say what a merge brings,
in terms of reachability, and name the

236
00:17:02,815 --> 00:17:07,548
read-only commands. If you can add what each
practice costs and when you would relax

237
00:17:07,588 --> 00:17:10,786
